+# Changes
+
+## Moved
+
+- `candidates/b/diff.mjs` -> `src/diff.mjs`, the final implementation's place
+  per `README.md`. It is self-contained (no imports) and exports `diffLines`.
+  `candidates/a`, `candidates/b` and `candidates/c` are untouched.
+
+## Changed from `candidates/b`
+
+- Removed the dead `max === 0` guard in `shortestEditTrace` (was
+  `candidates/b/diff.mjs:39-42`). `diffLines` already returns `[]` for two
+  empty inputs before calling `shortestEditTrace`, so the branch could never
+  run. Behaviour is unchanged.
+- Made that dependency explicit instead of implicit: the `shortestEditTrace`
+  doc comment now states it requires at least one non-empty input (so
+  `max >= 1`), and the both-empty early return in `diffLines` notes that it is
+  what provides that guarantee.
+- Everything else (validation, the forward trace, the backtrack, the
+  defensive `slice()` copies) is as in `candidates/b`.
+
+## Borrowed from `candidates/a`
+
+- The explicit statement of memory cost. `candidates/b` documented only the
+  O((N+M)·D) time bound; the header comment in `src/diff.mjs` now also states
+  the O((N+M)·D) space bound, explains where it comes from (one full
+  `Int32Array` frontier snapshot per edit distance, kept for the backtrack),
+  and gives the practical consequence (hundreds of megabytes for two unrelated
+  inputs of a few thousand lines; negligible for the usual small-D review
+  case). This was the one idea PICK.md flagged as worth borrowing, and it fits
+  as a comment-only addition with no code change.
